{"chunk_id": "b2e32e1127a4", "text": "This section depicts Arjuna\u2019s relentless push through the Kaurava forces while racing to fulfill his vow to kill Jayadratha. Drona repeatedly intercepts him, unleashing overwhelming showers of arrows and even momentarily overpowering his former pupil. Guided by Krishna, Arjuna avoids wasting time fighting his teacher directly and presses forward through successive defenders including Kritavarman and the Kamvojas. The most dramatic episode is the death of King Srutayudha, who wields a divine mace granted by Varuna with a fatal condition: it must never be hurled at a non\u2011combatant. In fury he throws it at Krishna, who is not fighting, and the enchanted weapon rebounds and kills its owner. The episode highlights Arjuna\u2019s unstoppable momentum, Krishna\u2019s strategic judgment, and the moral law that even divine weapons obey.\nArjuna battles Drona and multiple Kaurava warriors while pushing forward to fulfill his vow to kill Jayadratha; Srutayudha dies when his divine mace rebounds upon him.\nThemes: guru\u2013disciple conflict, battle prowess, fate and divine weapons, vengeance for Abhimanyu, advancing toward Jayadratha", "vector": [-0.008725238963961601, -0.00922966655343771, -0.01940002292394638, 0.022699253633618355, 0.007777732331305742, 0.02289011888206005, -0.01694604940712452, -0.007348286919295788, -0.03190165385603905, -0.027688998728990555, 0.009318281896412373, 0.012269866652786732, 0.017723141238093376, -0.0012142055202275515, 0.007375553250312805, 0.0028339982964098454, 0.03364670276641846, -0.013196923770010471, 0.02947494573891163, -0.03560987859964371, -0.008882020600140095, -0.008132195100188255, -0.008398042060434818, 0.01720508001744747, -0.005344208795577288, 0.0406268909573555, -0.007327836938202381, -0.03127452731132507, 0.012637962587177753, -0.01626439020037651, -0.01387858297675848, 0.0024488610215485096, 0.007198321633040905, -0.003929765895009041, -0.031874388456344604, -0.00109235895797610